<h1>IndoorLocate Android App</h1>

<p>
IndoorLocate is a <strong>final year engineering project</strong> designed
to identify the indoor location of a user such as a classroom or lab.
</p>

<div class="box">

<h2>📌 Problem</h2>

<p>
GPS signals are weak or unavailable inside buildings.
IndoorLocate solves this by using <strong>Wi-Fi router identifiers (BSSID)</strong>
to determine which room the user is currently located in.
</p>

</div>

<div class="box">

<h2>⚙️ How It Works</h2>

<ul>
<li>The Android app reads the Wi-Fi network information</li>
<li>It extracts the <strong>BSSID (router ID)</strong></li>
<li>The BSSID is sent to the server</li>
<li>The server maps the router to a specific classroom</li>
</ul>

</div>

<div class="box">

<h2>🔐 Privacy</h2>

<p>The app does not collect personal information.</p>

<ul>
<li>No contacts</li>
<li>No files</li>
<li>No camera or microphone</li>
<li>No identity tracking</li>
</ul>

<p>
Android requires location permission only to access Wi-Fi scan data.
</p>

